  "id": "canto_a_lo_poeta",
  "name": "Canto a lo poeta (Chilean sung décima, a lo divino and a lo humano)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung poetry of rural central Chile in ten-line décimas, divided into canto a lo divino, religious verse sung at vigils for saints and at wakes for dead infants (velorios de angelito), and canto a lo humano, secular verse on history, love and wisdom that includes the improvised paya contest. Cantores accompany themselves on the guitarrón chileno, a 25-string guitar with coursed metal strings and short drone strings (diablitos) beside the fingerboard, or on guitar, playing repeated melodic formulas (entonaciones). Pirque, near Santiago, is a centre of guitarrón playing; the twelve-string card stands in for the guitarrón.",
  "recipe": "classic modern canto a lo poeta, ballad Poetry, Latin am troubadour branch. one note per syllable, solo with instrumental accompaniment, unprocessed natural acoustic. acoustic guitar 12 string, classical nylon-string guitar. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
